// twice-capture — the k CAPTURE gate (refuter hole H1, band B k1).
//
// Both landing gates (mn-multishot, twice-handler-nonidentity) reify a k with
// ZERO captures (identity; a moved literal), so the closure-identical record
// head — captures at 8+4*i, where LUpval reads — and the whole
// resolve_captures_outer wiring are exercised by NEITHER. This one puts a
// genuine free local in the remainder: `z` is body's param, live at the
// perform, so k captures it by value and BOTH resumptions read it through
// the record.
//
// body(5): k = (v) => v + z with z=5 captured. k(10)=15, k(20)=25 → 40.
// Exit 40 (< 127, below the wasmtime exit-alias wall).
//
// Run (through a fixed m2):
//   MENTL_BOOT=.build/m2cache/m2.wasm tools/run-micro.sh \
//     tests/native-cont/twice-capture.mn 40 \
//     lib/memory.mn lib/strings.mn lib/lists.mn lib/prelude.mn

effect Pick { pick() -> Int }

handler twice with total = 0 {
  pick() => {
    let a = resume(10)
    let b = resume(20)
    a + b
  }
}

fn body(z) = pick() + z

fn main(q) = { body(5) } ~> twice
